Subject: [PATCH] docs: follow-up for task 33 (33A, 33B, 33C, 33D) and task 35
 (35A)

RUNBOOK 7.2 and 8.6: a failed replacement of witnesses.rec says "was
not replaced" for every failed rename and "is unchanged" only when the
temporary file failed, with the causes, the remedy and the limit on
NFS or FUSE; 7.3 and 8.6: the new message before the log, "opened and
removed leftover temporary files (.tmp-*) from; nothing written or
logged". RUNBOOK 0.2: check-release.sh checks the exit status of grep
and sort; TestReleaseSwitches searches directories named _*, .* and
testdata (and links of such names) for tagged files, with its messages
verbatim, searches .git and .claude/worktrees, skips entries that
vanish and confirms problems in a second walk 3 s later. DECISIONS:
addendum 33 A to D93. AUDIT: addendum 33g, R17 (b), R35, 6.2 (one new
row, two extended). HANDOFF: addendum 33g, run times of 33D, known
flakes (TestRelayBrokenPipe under -json), test rules for setNofile and
keepNofile and for descriptor 2 under go test -json, known limits, open
decisions (package 29B still unmerged, its commit lost; new V2, which
changes internal/keys). Backlog after M1: addendum 33g; 110, 118, 119
done; parts of 95, 108 and 121 done; 27 with the measurement 33D; new
123 to 125, 126 done with 35A. Hints of the review of 32g in the heads
of 32g: what the parent t in a subtest did (no panic for a subtest that
is not parallel, read in the source of testing in go1.26.10) and what
the head of 31g refers to.

